  <div class="lesson-content">

    <h2 class="lesson-heading">Why expose an agent as an HTTP service</h2>

    <p>
      The scripts from lessons 2–4 run on your machine from a terminal.
      An HTTP service means:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Any client — web app, mobile, Slack bot, another service — can talk to your agent</li>
      <li>Multiple users concurrently, each with their own thread</li>
      <li>NestJS handles request parsing, validation, error serialisation, and DI for free</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="lesson-heading">Module structure — 4 files, clear separation of concerns</h2>

    <LessonDiagram definition={`
flowchart TD
  C["POST /agent/chat\nHTTP client"]:::step --> A
  A["AgentController\nvalidates DTO · delegates"]:::step --> B
  B["AgentService\nagent loop + tool execution"]:::step --> R
  R["ThreadRepository\nload / save messages"]:::done
  B --> S["Anthropic SDK\n+ tools"]:::step

  classDef step fill:#dbeafe,color:#1e3a8a,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,color:#14532d,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    `} />

